From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] EDEN_UP_ASTC_BC1_ALL=1, a PICTURE TRADE: every re-compressed ASTC texture is BC1 instead of BC3 (1-bit alpha), half the memory of the alpha ones; off by default

Idea from Eglantine's #ocarina-of-time Discord, 9 Nov (Diethelm: Eglantine, NX2navi and Hookshot all
convert ASTC to BC3, BC1 cuts VRAM a lot; CandyBlue, RX 5600 XT 6 GB, got past the post-intro
out-of-memory crash with BC1). The BC1 mode is Eden's own ASTC recompression setting
(AstcRecompression::Bc1, yuzu 2023; CPU encoder BCN::CompressBC1 with the 0.5 alpha threshold).
The GPU encoder (bc_encoder.comp) already writes punch-through BC1 for the opaque path. The PS5
had no way to pick it: the setting stays at its BC3 default and the console has no config UI.

What it does: TextureCacheRuntime's constructor, right after UseBc3ForSwitch2OnSmallCards and
before anything reads the setting (passes, view formats), sets the recompression override to Bc1
when the switch is exactly "1", the device has no native ASTC and the session is BC3. Every
place already follows Settings::GetAstcRecompression(): host and view formats (maxwell_to_vk),
host bytes and the TEX_TRIM decision (HostBytesFromLevel), the CPU path's buffer sizes and
encoder (CalculateConvertedSizeBytes, ConvertedLayout, ConvertImage), the GPU transcode's encode
mode and output buffer (bc3 = false), TranscodedAstcSize. Startup only, never flipped later.
The switch name joins the shader-prep stamp list (generated from the backend's names), so the
first run with it builds its own shader-prep store.

PICTURE TRADE. Only the alpha ASTC changes (opaque ASTC is BC1 already, EDEN_NX2_ASTC_BC1).
Alpha becomes 1 bit at about 0.5: soft alpha (smoke, fog cards, light shafts, glows, fades,
anti-aliased text and HUD edges) gets hard edges, and a transparent texel decodes as black, so
straight-alpha filtering can leave dark fringes. Blocks with any transparent texel have three
colours instead of four, which bands more. Both encoders also drop the colour of a texel under
0.5 alpha (CompressBCN zeroes it, bc_encoder.comp picks the transparent index), so a texture
that keeps data in alpha instead of coverage (blend masks, terrain weights) shows black or
wrongly blended patches wherever that alpha is under 0.5, not only hard edges: look at the
6144 ground texture and the format-71 array first, the two biggest alpha ASTC images. Never for
the play env until the picture is judged.

Memory, Ocarina of Time (t85-f run702 village walk, control):
- 6144x6144 13-level ground texture: 48 -> 24 MiB kept, and its GPU transcode output buffer
  48 -> 24 MiB. The RGBA8 decode image is the same (192 MiB), so EDEN_NX2_GPU_TRANSCODE_MIB
  routes it as before.
- Format-71 1365x1365x90 array: 213 -> 106 MiB, after EDEN_NX2_TEX_TRIM_MIB=64 53 -> 27 MiB
  (still over 64, still trimmed). The format-60 array is BC1 already.
- The other alpha ASTC: about 62% of new ASTC images (584 alpha / 361 opaque per 600 frames),
  half their bytes. The log counts images, not bytes per format: about 50 MiB is certain, 100-300
  MiB in the village is the estimate.
- No opaque scan runs, so the texture cache's astc_scan_buffer (grown to the largest scanned
  ASTC image, up to 64 MiB, never shrunk) stays empty.
- The 6144's GPU transcode output only matters with EDEN_NX2_GPU_TRANSCODE_MIB over 192; at the
  default 128 it takes the CPU decode, whose output buffer halves the same way.

Testing: the first run with the switch has no kept shader translations (its own stamp), so prime
the store with one run before comparing memory or stutter against the control.

Interplay:
- EDEN_NX2_TC_KEEP_ASYNC: AsynchronousDecode is still set by the RGBA8 scratch size
  (TranscodeScratchTooLarge), so the same images are kept; each kept one is half the size, and
  the CPU decode's output buffer halves (fewer "No memory to decode" retries expected).
- EDEN_NX2_GPU_TRANSCODE_MIB: routing unchanged (it measures the decode image); only the encode
  output halves. The 6144's gap in KEEP_ASYNC at =256 stays: this switch does not close it.
- Ahead guard (0491-0504): covers buffer pages and constant-buffer reads only, no texture
  formats. No interaction.
- EDEN_UP_SKIP_STALE_UPLOADS (0495): CopiesWriteWholeImage already refuses block-compressed
  formats and compares astc_opaque, which is false on both sides here. No interaction.
- EDEN_NX2_AREA_EVICT: counts images, not bytes; bursts free less per image because images are
  smaller. No change needed.
- EDEN_UP_ASTC_BATCH_MIB (draft): sizes its output by the same bc3 flag, so BC1 halves its
  output batches too. Textually independent.
- The opaque scan does not run with the switch (nothing to choose), so the TC_LOG line shows
  "ASTC 0 opaque / 0 alpha". EDEN_NX2_ASTC_BC1=0 has no effect while it is on. Huge arrays and
  EDEN_NX2_UNEVEN_MIPS_RGBA8 images stay RGBA8. A future alpha array of 64-128 MiB as BC3 would
  drop under TEX_TRIM_MIB=64 as BC1 and keep its top level (none in run702: only the two 1365
  arrays are trimmed).

Unset (or anything but "1"): no override, byte for byte as before. Nothing compiled or run.

---
diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_prep.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_prep.cpp
index 6b75745..e91d6fb 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_prep.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_prep.cpp
@@ -126,7 +126,8 @@ constexpr const char* TranslationSwitches[] = {
     "EDEN_PE_PIPELINE_CACHE_EXIT", "EDEN_PE_REG_BLOCKS", "EDEN_PE_STATIC_VERTEX_INPUT",
     "EDEN_PE_TRANSCODE_BOUND", "EDEN_PE_UNIFORM_PREFETCH", "EDEN_PE_VMA_OWN_BUDGET",
     "EDEN_PS5_LAZY_PRESENT", "EDEN_PS5_TRANSCODE_PENDING_MIB", "EDEN_STREAMLINE_DIR",
-    "EDEN_STREAM_RING_MIB", "EDEN_TC_SCRATCH_KEEP_MIB", "EDEN_UP_BACK_DRAW_CHEAP",
+    "EDEN_STREAM_RING_MIB", "EDEN_TC_SCRATCH_KEEP_MIB", "EDEN_UP_ASTC_BC1_ALL",
+    "EDEN_UP_BACK_DRAW_CHEAP",
     "EDEN_UP_BIND_ON_BACK", "EDEN_UP_BLIT_EDGE_CLAMP", "EDEN_UP_BUFFER_USE_MARKS",
     "EDEN_UP_COMPUTE_INDIRECT_ORDER", "EDEN_UP_DEFERRED_CLEAR_PASS", "EDEN_UP_DJ_CHANNEL_IDS",
     "EDEN_UP_DJ_FRAG_BARRIER", "EDEN_UP_DJ_GATHER_OWNERS", "EDEN_UP_DRAIN_SKIP_SAME",
diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.cpp
index f1766f2..87012cd 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.cpp
@@ -1378,6 +1378,29 @@ void UseBc3ForSwitch2OnSmallCards(const Device& device) {
                 memory >> 20);
     Settings::SetAstcRecompressionOverride(Settings::AstcRecompression::Bc3);
 }
+
+// EDEN_UP_ASTC_BC1_ALL=1 (Common::PeSwitch, exact "1", read once; off by default). A PICTURE
+// TRADE: every ASTC texture that would be re-compressed to BC3 goes to BC1 instead, half the
+// memory. BC1 keeps one bit of alpha: a texel under 0.5 alpha becomes transparent black, one at or
+// over it fully opaque, so soft alpha (smoke, fog cards, light shafts, glows, fades, text edges)
+// gets hard, possibly dark-fringed edges, and colour blocks with any transparent texel have three
+// colours instead of four. Opaque ASTC is BC1 already (EDEN_NX2_ASTC_BC1), so only the alpha
+// textures change. Both encoders already write punch-through BC1 (bc_encoder.comp,
+// BCN::CompressBC1), and every size and format choice follows Settings::GetAstcRecompression().
+// Set before any image exists and never changed later: a texture made as BC3 must not be
+// re-uploaded as BC1. Huge arrays and EDEN_NX2_UNEVEN_MIPS_RGBA8 images stay RGBA8, an
+// uncompressed session stays uncompressed, and EDEN_NX2_ASTC_BC1=0 no longer applies.
+void UseBc1ForAllAstc(const Device& device) {
+    static const bool enabled = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_ASTC_BC1_ALL");
+    if (!enabled || device.IsOptimalAstcSupported() ||
+        Settings::GetAstcRecompression() != Settings::AstcRecompression::Bc3) {
+        return;
+    }
+    LOG_WARNING(Render_Vulkan,
+                "EDEN_UP_ASTC_BC1_ALL: every re-compressed ASTC texture is BC1 for this session, "
+                "alpha ones included (picture trade: 1-bit alpha at 0.5)");
+    Settings::SetAstcRecompressionOverride(Settings::AstcRecompression::Bc1);
+}
 } // Anonymous namespace
 
 TextureCacheRuntime::TextureCacheRuntime(const Device& device_, Scheduler& scheduler_,
@@ -1394,6 +1417,7 @@ TextureCacheRuntime::TextureCacheRuntime(const Device& device_, Scheduler& sched
       resolution{Settings::values.resolution_info} {
     // Before anything below reads astc_recompression (passes, view formats).
     UseBc3ForSwitch2OnSmallCards(device);
+    UseBc1ForAllAstc(device);
     // Huge ASTC arrays always decode on the GPU (IsHugeAstcArray), whatever the decode setting.
     if (Settings::values.accelerate_astc.GetValue() == Settings::AstcDecodeMode::Gpu ||
         !device.IsOptimalAstcSupported()) {
